course: dictionary
lesson: 15153
title: Schoolteacher
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A schoolteacher is a person whose job is teaching children in a school. The word is made from two parts you already know, school and teacher. When you see it, think of a teacher who works in a school.
explain: Read the words around it to check. «Mrs Patel is a schoolteacher at our local primary school.» The words at our local primary school tell you where she works. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Teacher fits, but schoolteacher tells you the school part as well.
explain: Schoolteacher can name a job in everyday life and in stories, often in a village or small school. «My aunt was a schoolteacher for thirty years before she retired.» Retired means she stopped working, so she had taught children for a long time. Being a schoolteacher is a career that needs training.
fact: A schoolteacher is a person whose job is teaching children in a school.
fact: Schoolteacher is written as one word, made from school and teacher.
fact: The plural is schoolteachers, as in «Two schoolteachers ran the school fair.»
fact: «A primary schoolteacher» teaches children in a primary school.
fact: «A retired schoolteacher» is someone who used to teach and no longer works.
exercise: «Mrs Patel is a schoolteacher at our local primary school.» What is a schoolteacher? | A child who goes to school | A person who sells food in a shop | *A person whose job is teaching children in a school | A building where people sleep
exercise: Which phrase means a teacher who has stopped working? | a school bell | a primary schoolteacher | *a retired schoolteacher | a schoolteacher's bag
exercise: What is the plural of schoolteacher? | schoolteacher's | schoolteacheres | schoolteach | *schoolteachers
test: Ben's mum is a schoolteacher. What does Ben's mum do for work? | She drives the school bus | She cooks dinner in a school kitchen | *She teaches children in a school | She cleans the classrooms
test: Which of these is written correctly as one word? | *schoolteacher | school teacher | school-teacher-ing | teacher school
exam: Which sentence uses schoolteacher correctly? | «She went to schoolteacher to buy bread.» | «The schoolteacher is a loud bus that drives fast.» | «The schoolteacher sang the rain away.» | *«Our schoolteacher reads us a story after lunch.»
